# =========================================================
# AGENT IDENTITY
# =========================================================
# The gateway generates a development CA and agents store their own keys.
# `backend/data/` already covers the defaults; these catch a configured
# AGENT_IDENTITY_DIR pointed somewhere else in the tree. Committing a CA
# private key is the one mistake in this milestone that cannot be undone by
# a follow-up commit.
agent_identity/
enrolment.json
*.key
!**/testdata/**/*.key

# =========================================================
# INVESTIGATION REPORTS WRITTEN AT THE REPOSITORY ROOT
# =========================================================
# `FilesystemReportStore` writes to a **relative** `data/investigations`, so
# where the reports land is decided by the working directory the backend was
# started from. `backend/.gitignore` covers the documented case; started from
# the repository root instead — which every `scripts/*_bench.py` does, since
# they are run from there — it writes here, and nothing covered that.
#
# Four report artefacts from a failed investigation were already committed
# this way, swept into the v0.2.3 release commit by a `git add`. That one
# reached no cluster, so it carried nothing; the same accident on an
# investigation that *had* connected would have committed pod names,
# namespaces and log lines to a public repository.
/data/
